        <header>
          <span class="badge badge--danger">Announcement</span>
          <time datetime="2026-10-05" class="muted small">5 October 2026</time>
        </header>
        <h3>Registration hits 70 percent capacity</h3>
        <p>Eighty-nine of the 128 team seats are now filled, with the AI &amp; Data track closest to
          selling out. If your team is still deciding, lock in a provisional seat before 20 November so
          you keep your preferred track.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href="register.html">Reserve a seat &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="post">
        <header>
          <span class="badge">Programme</span>
          <time datetime="2026-09-28" class="muted small">28 September 2026</time>
        </header>
        <h3>Mentor line-up confirmed: 24 engineers across six tracks</h3>
        <p>Partner desks are finalised. Each track gets four dedicated mentors plus two floating
          reviewers who attend the mid-build showcase. Office-hour slots open on the participant
          dashboard one week before kickoff.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href="sponsors.html">Meet the partners &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="post">
        <header>
          <span class="badge badge--accent">Deadline</span>
          <time datetime="2026-09-21" class="muted small">21 September 2026</time>
        </header>
        <h3>Design sprint entries close 20 November</h3>
        <p>The 90-minute UI Design Sprint runs alongside the hackathon and takes individual or paired
          entries. It is the best way to compete if you prefer Figma to JavaScript, and the judging
          rubric is published in the resources library.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href="activities.html">See the side competitions &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="post">
        <header>
          <span class="badge badge--ok">Blog</span>
          <time datetime="2026-09-14" class="muted small">14 September 2026</time>
        </header>
        <h3>How to scope a 48-hour project in one hour</h3>
        <p>Our technical lead's checklist: cut the database, mock the data, pick one user role, define
          the single happy path, and only then decide what delight you can afford. Teams that follow
          this order finish; teams that do not spend Sunday morning rewriting migrations.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href="resources.html">Download the build log template &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="post">
        <header>
          <span class="badge">Committee</span>
          <time datetime="2026-09-07" class="muted small">7 September 2026</time>
        </header>
        <h3>Registration is officially open</h3>
        <p>The Nexus committee opened registration for the 2026 edition after the semester break. The
          briefing session for registered teams runs online on 1 December at 18:00 and recording will be
          posted here.</p>
        <p class="small"><a href="register.html">Register a team &rarr;</a></p>
      </article>
